WEBVTT

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:32.800
<i>Okay.</i>

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.310
I'm Sakura Kinomoto.

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.580
<i>I started my first year at Tomoeda 
Middle School this spring.</i>

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:52.230
<i>I'm still terrible at math,</i>

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:56.160
<i>but I enjoy my studies and my club, 
and I keep busy every day.</i>

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:02.850
<b>Sakura, the Rabbit, and the Song of the Moon</b>

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.840
The flowers have all fallen, 
but it's so pretty!

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:14.190
Our flower-viewing party was so much fun.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.370
<i>Syaoran-kun was there, too...</i>

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.240
It's great.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.260
Jealous... So jealous...

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.860
I'm so jealous!

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:27.510
Kero-chan!

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:31.380
Flower viewing sounds so fun! 
I wanted to go, too!

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.140
Kero-chan, weren't you staying home?

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.840
I stayed home when you 
went to see the flowers!

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:42.490
But you were so happy when you got 
to eat the sweets I brought home.

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:45.010
Well, that was that, and this is this.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:49.060
If it'd only been Tomoyo-chan and Syaoran-kun, 
it would've been okay.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.740
By the way, the new girl 
was also there, right?

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.520
Yeah, Akiho-chan!

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.400
She's the one who gave me those sweets.

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:59.160
All right! She's a great girl!

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.500
She really is.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:06.540
Also, after we ate, Tomoyo-chan sang for us.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.590
Oh, that sounds nice.

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:10.810
It was so beautiful...

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:12.950
I should have recorded it.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:14.300
Didn't you have your smartphone?

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:16.650
I didn't think of it until later.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:22.920
I wish there were a way to record things instantly, 
the moment you decide you want to.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:27.610
Then you'd never have to miss a 
shot of my good-looking face.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:30.160
You have a smartphone too, don't you?

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:31.440
Yep!

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:35.410
Isn't Tomoyo-chan's mom's company amazing?

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:39.200
They're not just about toys. They sell 
smartphones and computers, as well.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.310
Their headsets are really good, too!

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.960
Right, you use yours to play 
video games, all the time...

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.060
I'm gonna beat Spinny next time!

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:48.480
Whoops.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:55.410
Oh, it's Akiho-chan!

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:56.910
Akiho-chan!

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.380
Sakura-san!

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:01.770
Hi!

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.320
Hello. Are you running errands?

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.480
Yeah, I'm getting stuff to cook for dinner.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:07.750
How about you?

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:08.890
Same here!

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.110
But since I just moved here,

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:14.240
I don't know where I should shop.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.780
Then let's go together! 
I'll show you the way!

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:19.600
Thank you!

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:24.650
Do you always do the shopping?

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:26.940
No, the person I live with...

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.700
The one who's important to you?

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.480
Yes, ah... but, um...

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.750
He does some shopping, too.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:37.270
So I wanted to help him out, however I could.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:38.710
That's really nice of you.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:43.620
It's all I can do for him, really.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:48.380
You really love this person, huh?

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:04.020
What a cute bunny.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.470
I always keep it with me.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:09.770
But I don't know if it's okay 
if I bring it to school...

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:12.590
I wanted to bring it with
me to our flower-viewing party,

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:14.120
but I thought it might be too childish.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.600
Not at all! Our school 
allows things like that!

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.960
Everyone would rave about how cute it is.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.790
I always have Kero—

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:23.750
Kero?

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:25.600
U-Um, I mean...

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.580
I... I have a stuffed animal called 
Kero-chan that means a lot to me!

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:29.800
So we're the same!

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:30.920
Yep!

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.680
Starting tomorrow, I'll bring 
mine with me to school.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:35.680
How about you?

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.680
Huh? Um, I...

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.370
S-Sure! I'll bring Kero-chan!

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:46.700
Does yours have a name?

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.540
Yes, it's Momo.

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:52.900
Hi, I'm Sakura. Momo-chan, 
let's be friends, okay?

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:55.790
I hope you two will be friends, too.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:57.540
Right, Momo?

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:00.990
I'm home.

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:05.300
Welcome home, Sakura-san.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.370
You're home? What about school?

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:11.310
I have to go back tonight...

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:13.940
But I needed to get some materials here.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:16.870
I see.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:25.730
I'm home, Mom!

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:30.260
Been shopping?

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.130
It's my turn to make dinner tonight.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:35.760
You're making potatoes au gratin tonight?

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:36.560
Bingo!

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.280
Ah, and rolled omelets, too.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:39.900
Those are for lunch tomorrow.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:43.710
<b>Fujitaka: Home around 5:00...? 
Will leave a message. 
Toya: School, then work. 
Dinner at home. 
Sakura: Home by 4:00.</b>

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:43.440
Speaking of, you wrote the time 
you'd be home on the board...

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:45.960
Sorry I'm a little late.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.490
It's all right, but did you 
need to do something?

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:53.160
I ran into a friend, and we 
went shopping together.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:54.790
It was the transfer student I told you about.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.690
Ah, the one who's been to 
lots of different countries?

00:06:59.040 --> 00:06:59.910
Yeah!

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.560
<b>Meiling-chan</b>

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:03.570
Here.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:06.680
<i>Heya!</i>

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:08.890
Hi, Meiling-chan!

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:11.400
<i>I see you never change, Kinomoto-san.</i>

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:14.730
<i>You're always spacing out.</i>

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:16.430
Y-You think so?

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.630
<i>Is this a good time to talk?</i>

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:21.350
<i>It's around dinnertime there, isn't it?</i>

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:24.040
I still have time. 
What time is it in Hong Kong?

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.940
<i>I told you before, remember?</i>

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:28.340
<i>It's just an hour behind Japan!</i>

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.870
<i>I was just relaxing and having a snack.</i>

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:33.320
Aw, peach manju! Lucky!

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.160
<i>Yum!</i>

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:41.060
You're still such an evil brat...

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.480
<i>And I see you're still a little runt.</i>

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.770
What'd you say?!

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:49.060
What's runty about this body, huh?!

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:51.490
Just look at how good-looking I am!

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:53.340
<i>You're too big. You're blocking the view.</i>

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:54.740
You little brat!

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:57.390
Y-You <i>are</i> kind of in the way—

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.490
Not you, too!

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.150
<i>Putting aside your space-wasting 
stuffed animal...</i>

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.780
Don't put me aside, fool!

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:03.230
<i>Is Syaoran doing okay?</i>

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:04.510
Don't ignore me!

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:09.860
I'm not a stuffed animal! 
Just see at how awesome I look!

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:08.620
Yeah. He said he'd wait to join a 
club until things settled down,

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:10.390
but he's enjoying school.

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:13.940
<i>Well, I'm sure he is. He's near 
a certain someone, after all.</i>

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:18.530
<i>You really haven't changed...</i>

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:21.260
Well, that's Sakura for ya.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:25.030
<i>I guess Syaoran will still 
have it rough for a while.</i>

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:28.650
Aren't you gonna come visit?

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:31.800
<i>I have school, too, so I can't right away.</i>

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.740
<i>But I plan to visit Japan over summer break.</i>

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:35.610
Really?

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:38.860
<i>You'd better show me all 
the best spots, okay?</i>

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:40.030
I'll try!

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:44.190
And I'll give ya some one-on-one training, 
so come prepared, little girl!

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.920
<i>I'll beat you at your own game!</i>

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:46.870
Hah!

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:48.440
<i>Well, talk to you later!</i>

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.150
Okay, later.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.050
<b>Meiling-chan 
Call Ended</b>

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.960
I'll get to see Meiling-chan!

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.480
Oh, I have to tell Tomoyo-chan!

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:02.450
Where should we go?

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:05.560
We should go somewhere 
Meiling-chan hasn't been yet...

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:09.310
Don't forget to film it 
when you do, all right?

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:11.270
Sure.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:21.730
It's very good.

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:22.740
I'm so glad!

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:24.790
Not bad.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:26.620
Jeez!

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:30.080
Dad, are you leaving right after you eat?

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:33.060
Yeah, and I think I'll be there overnight.

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:34.520
You're pretty busy, huh?

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:36.570
There's a conference coming up.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:39.870
Some students will be presenting 
their theses for the first time,

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:43.030
so I want to be there for them, 
as much as possible.

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:45.510
Take care of your health, okay?

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:46.640
Thanks.

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:50.200
Classic mistake...

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.080
Better get a picture of this.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.870
Don't!

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.070
<b>Gotta show Yuki.</b>

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:57.150
Ugh!

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:59.810
Seriously, you're always so mean to me!

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:06.830
What's wrong, Sakura-san?

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:20.330
It's you again!

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:28.390
Do you want to say something to me?

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:29.990
Do you want my key?

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:36.790
<i>A clock...</i>

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:48.950
Who are you?

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:54.440
Who?!

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:56.390
Sakura-san?

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:00.190
Are you okay?

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.560
Did I... fall asleep?

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:06.770
No, but you didn't answer when I spoke to you.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:10.830
Sorry! I guess I spaced out!

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:13.170
I'll cut some more bread!

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:27.500
Morning!

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.500
Good morning!

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:33.160
Yo!

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:35.530
Kero-chan is with you?

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:38.370
Yesterday, I promised Akiho-chan to bring him.

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:40.630
Akiho-chan?

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:45.040
I see. So that's why Kero-chan is with you.

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:49.890
He's pretty big, so he'd stand out if I 
put him on the outside of my bag.

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:53.100
Maybe, but was this really the answer?

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:57.810
I know having a mascot bigger than the 
smartphone it's attached to is odd, but...

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:59.100
You look cute.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:00.730
Really?!

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:02.610
You're so easy to please.

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:14.430
"...bubbled up in a searing red hue.

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:20.490
The ship gave a fearsome 
roar and chased after it,

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:23.470
<b>Ten Nights of Dreams 
Natsume Soseki</b>

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:23.460
but it never caught up.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:28.840
At one point, I caught a man with 
the ship's crew and asked him,

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:32.590
'Is this ship heading west?'

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:39.100
The man gave me a dubious look and 
stared at me for some time.

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:42.150
Eventually, he asked me, 'Why?'

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:47.120
<b>Japanese 1</b>

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:45.460
'Because it seems to be 
pursuing the sunset.'"

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:47.100
Okay! You can stop there!

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:49.510
Thank you, Kinomoto-san.

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:54.250
All of the dream stories gathered in 
<i>Ten Nights of Dreams</i> are strange,

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.130
just like this one.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:59.710
There are a few that some 
might even consider scary.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:08.140
<b>Ten Nights of Dreams 
Natsume Soseki</b>

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:05.170
Now, did you know there's a kind 
of dream called a "premonition"?

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:08.130
They're dreams in which you see 
things happening in the future.

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:11.770
The dreams in <i>Ten Nights of Dreams </i>
are not necessarily premonitions...

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:10.860
<i>Premonitions?</i>

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:15.240
<i>What was that dream?</i>

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:22.150
<i>Before, I dreamed about 
Mizuki-sensei and Eriol-kun, too.</i>

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:24.280
<b>Ten Nights of Dreams 
Natsume Soseki</b>

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:24.280
Now, Shinomoto-san, 
please read the next part.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:25.060
Huh?

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:29.920
You can do it, Akiho-chan.

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:41.810
"Then the crew man laughed loudly

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:44.760
and walked away from me.

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:48.110
'Does the sun travel west 
to end up in the east?

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:49.790
Is that true?

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:52.940
Does the sun that rises in the 
east originate in the west?

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:54.810
Is that true?

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:57.990
I stand above waves, with a 
rudder as my pillow.

00:13:57.990 --> 00:13:59.230
Float it. Float it.'"

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:02.710
I'm so hungry!

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:03.860
Where should we eat?

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.730
I made my own lunch today.

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:10.590
Akiho-chan!

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:14.900
You were great with the reading!

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:16.620
Did I read it right?

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.320
It was wonderful.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:20.620
Uh-huh!

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:24.550
By the way, Akiho-chan, have you 
decided on a club yet?

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:27.310
I'm still having trouble deciding.

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:30.100
Tomoeda Middle School does 
have a Theater Club.

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:32.990
I mean, your reading of that 
passage was really good!

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:34.760
The one Naoko-san is in?

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:35.760
Yeah!

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:39.270
And you two are in the 
Cheerleading Club, right?

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.000
Yep. Want to try it with us?

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:44.370
I've never done anything like that.

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:47.980
That's okay! A lot of girls in 
the club started this year!

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:49.540
Right.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:51.430
How about the Chorus Club?

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:04.610
Li-kun!

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:06.780
What is it?

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:10.820
If you aren't in a hurry, 
could you come with me?

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:38.880
I got the teacher's permission to borrow 
this room over the lunch break!

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:40.390
Akiho-chan...

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:41.190
Yes?

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:44.100
You sang at our flower viewing, remember?

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:45.840
Y-Yes...

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:50.000
And I could hear you singing 
along when I sang.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:52.090
I heard it, too!

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:54.350
You have such a sweet, clear voice.

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:57.460
I-I'm sorry for butting in on your song!

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.990
It made me happy.

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:05.050
Would you like to try singing with me here?

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:09.110
B-But I haven't sung in front of people much.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.110
I might not be very good.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.860
I wanna hear it!

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:13.660
Me, too!

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.140
Come on, sing!

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:17.410
Please do.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:19.970
I-I'll try.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:27.340
<b>Misty Moonlight</b>

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:26.980
Do you know this song, Akiho-chan?

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:30.580
I do!

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:34.590
I memorized this song when 
I was learning Japanese.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:35.710
I love it!

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:38.710
Li-kun?

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:41.440
Would you play the accompaniment?

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:42.950
Me?

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:45.290
I've heard you're very good.

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:46.200
From who?

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:47.770
Meiling-chan!

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:49.940
That girl...

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.700
Syaoran-kun, you can play piano?

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:54.690
I'm not that good.

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:55.750
I want to hear it!

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:59.480
Don't blame me if you can't sing along to it.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:25.900
<i>The light of sunset grows dim 
over the rape blossom field</i>

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:35.840
<i>The outlines of the mountains 
fade into the mist</i>

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:46.080
<i>In the calm spring breeze, 
I look up at the sky</i>

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:56.370
<i>A faint scent fills the air, 
beneath the evening moon</i>

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:16.680
<i>The lights of the town, 
the colors of the forest</i>

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:27.460
<i>The people walking through the rice fields</i>

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:37.470
<i>The calls of frogs, and the ringing of bells</i>

00:18:37.890 --> 00:18:48.370
<i>All grow hazy in the misty moonlight</i>

00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:11.260
That was great!

00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:14.370
It's a shame we were the 
only ones here to hear it!

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:16.330
Yeah, it was beautiful!

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:19.410
Only because Tomoyo-san took the lead for me.

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:22.840
It's because you sing so 
beautifully, Akiho-chan.

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:26.690
Your accompaniment was very 
easy to sing along to.

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:28.460
Thank you so much!

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:29.810
Uh, no problem...

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:33.140
Y-Yeah.

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:36.080
Yeah, the Chorus Club would be perfect!

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:38.910
I want to hear you two sing another duet!

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:41.170
It wouldn't be a bother if I joined?

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:44.010
I'm sure it would make everyone happy!

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:48.280
I'd like to join the Chorus Club!

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.860
You'd be very welcome.

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:54.170
That was the most beautiful "Misty 
Moonlight" I've ever heard!

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:55.120
Huh?

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:58.660
If cheerleading practice ends early, 
I might come visit the Chorus Club!

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:01.840
I'll invite Naoko-chan, too!

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:02.230
What is it?

00:20:02.770 --> 00:20:04.380
I don't know.

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:07.830
I can't quite tell... But I heard a sound.

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:09.440
A sound?

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:13.890
Did you learn any other Japanese songs?

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:12.910
Daidouji.

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:13.890
Yes?

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:16.060
Can we keep using this room?

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:20.820
The teacher said we could use it throughout 
lunch, so there's still time.

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:24.660
There's something I need 
to do. Can I borrow it?

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:27.400
All right.

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:31.660
Akiho-chan, let's go get 
a club application form.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:33.400
What? Right now?

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:34.360
Let's go!

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:35.080
Okay.

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.600
Hey, aren't those two coming?

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:39.310
They have other things to do.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.480
What's this about a sound?

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:52.070
I heard it during dinner last night, too.

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:53.810
What does it sound like?

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:57.300
Sort of... a humming.

00:20:57.300 --> 00:20:59.290
I've heard something like it before...

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:02.660
Oh! Like Tomoyo-chan's old camcorder!

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:03.650
A camcorder?

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:06.650
But where's it coming from?

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.550
There!

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:23.190
<i>Key that hides the forces of dreams!</i>

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:27.460
<i>Show me your true form!</i>

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:30.580
<i>Release!</i>

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:52.540
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:56.070
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:21:56.850 --> 00:21:58.040
<i>Secure!</i>

00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:13.280
Record...

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:17.310
<b>Record</b>

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:16.650
"Record."

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:20.890
I got another new card.

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:24.300
I didn't feel anything.

00:22:25.230 --> 00:22:28.240
This is nothing like when we 
collected the Clow Cards.

00:22:28.240 --> 00:22:30.240
Syaoran-kun?

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:36.640
I didn't feel... anything.

00:24:10.100 --> 00:24:12.410
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:15.140
It's the segment you gotta watch 
before you can get anywhere,

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:20.560
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:20.560
<b>K</b>

00:24:15.140 --> 00:24:16.140
Leave It to Kero-chan!

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:17.260
And this time...

00:24:17.260 --> 00:24:20.790
Here it is! One of the battle 
costumes we all love!

00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:23.200
She wore this when capturing the Action card.

00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:25.370
Its print of peaches and lotuses is

00:24:25.370 --> 00:24:27.440
the perfect balance of Japanese and Chinese.

00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:31.170
Speaking of peaches, I knew a guy who 
ate a peach and was scolded by God.

00:24:30.440 --> 00:24:31.450
<b>Goku?! 
You've met him?!</b>

00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:32.310
That monkey guy...

00:24:31.450 --> 00:24:37.240
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:31.450 --> 00:24:37.240
<b>K</b>

00:24:32.310 --> 00:24:35.780
Anyway, who knew that kid 
was so good at the piano?

00:24:35.780 --> 00:24:38.640
I can't let him beat me! 
Gotta think of my own special move!

00:24:38.640 --> 00:24:39.990
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.250
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.600 --> 00:24:44.500
Tomoyo-chan invited me to her house 
and showed me her new camera.

00:24:46.090 --> 00:24:48.040
It's so small, but does such amazing things!

00:24:48.050 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura and a Game of Tag in the Garden</b>

00:24:48.490 --> 00:24:51.560
Next time, "Sakura and a 
Game of Tag in the Garden."

00:24:51.560 --> 00:24:54.580
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.020
<b>End</b>
